From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:43:10 +0000
Subject: fast-listings: a folder's entries in one call, and RomFS files read
 ahead

On an exFAT drive (macOS's FSKit driver) a stat or an open by name costs
5-12 ms in a large folder: Mario Kart World's dump (411,696 files, 107,232
in romfs/Tex) was walked four times at a stat per file before its image
was written, over 10 minutes a walk, and its files were read one at a time.

romfs_image.listing() lists a folder with getattrlistbulk on macOS (name,
type, inode, size, mtime, ctime in one call per folder; os.scandir
elsewhere). children() keeps each file's identity for source_digest, which
matches os.stat exactly (checked on the dump), so existing stamps stay
valid. tree_size() in build_ipa_from_nsp.py uses it too. pack() reads
files up to 1 MB ahead on 16 threads. Each walk of the dump: 17 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
